  "evidence": [
    "Coordinator authorizes test-only follow-up for actual inline header destruction and the five complete RadioButton phase bindings now hosted by Dialogs. Preserve fixed historical checkpoints, identity/history comparisons and behavioral mutants. The preexisting Dialogs::close 0x612960 extraction repair must receive its own exact empty-body/identity/span/claim guard, not a blanket extraction waiver. Original task baseline and all C++ scopes remain unchanged.",
    "Pinned RadioButton constructor/table/phase relationships are already source-owned. Original406A90 is83-byte non-deleting phase and406F60 is130-byte scalar deleting phase; three original deleting adjustors406F50/407060/407080 tail into the latter.",
    "One native source-preserving overlay defining virtual ~RadioButton(){close();} in the real class header reproduces all five original phases in the genuine Dialogs owner object:406A90 is BYTE_EXACT under both profiles;406F60 and all three adjustors are BYTE_EXACT under application profile1. Jackal RadioButton object loses separate406A90 and emits127-byte deleting body under profile0. This demonstrates current compiler-source emission, not original source/TU spelling or final-link retained selection.",
    "Move all five existing FILE mappings with complete identities/spans/claims/history into dialogs.cpp through the native source writer, where real class usage emits them. Header owns the actual C++ destructor body, not a stand-in or hand-installed table. Keep existing RadioButton layout, bases, fields, close behavior and all other implementations unchanged. No flag changes, demotions, artificial emit anchors, compatibility wrappers, original-address calls or assembly.",
    "Task covers existing RadioButton and Dialogs ownership groups for dependent lifetime/compiler-output review. No unrelated implementation edits; report any other affected current owner/discovery centrally for explicit scope expansion. Actual source symbol/phase identities and all historical restoration obligations remain. Native build/link, scoped matching and mapped targets, outside-class observations, whole claim continuity and independent review are required before coordinator-reviewed manual integration; automatic/full-game acceptance stays unproven."
  ]
